WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.900
Sibač, a little village in the Pećinci municipality, which is located not far from three big cities.

2
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.040
On one side there's Šabac, on another Novi Sad,

3
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.920
and on the third — the capital, which in kilometers is the closest of all.

4
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.960
Sibač's strategic position gave its residents numerous advantages.

5
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.540
They had the best of both worlds: the quiet life of the countryside,

6
00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:29.320
and also the proximity of the big urban jungle, if anything is needed.

7
00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:34.580
That's why the residents of Sibač had no need to leave this little place,

8
00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:38.900
and the Nebrigić family has been enjoying the benefits of this town for decades.

9
00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:45.040
Well, it was poor, like all the other villages, it was poor,

10
00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:51.100
there was no asphalt, no sidewalks either, water, sewage.

11
00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:55.320
Today we have all of that.

12
00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:00.660
Yes, we have our own infrastructure and sewage system.

13
00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:04.320
And they did the reconstruction of the power grid for us.

14
00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:11.040
We have a post office, one good big store of our municipality head, it's his company.

15
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:15.920
He supplies fruit, vegetables and everything else needed.

16
00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:20.300
There are various suppliers here — both Šabac, and Belgrade, and Novi Sad.

17
00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:24.520
In short, we have everything here, we don't need to go anywhere from the village.

18
00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:30.660
And if we want to, there, next to us are Šabac, Belgrade, I'm telling you, Zemun.

19
00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:33.200
There, everything is near us.

20
00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:36.020
We go to Belgrade less often now because of traffic jams.

21
00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.820
We can no longer drive, neither I nor he,

22
00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:43.720
getting into those stressful situations there.

23
00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:47.340
Perhaps at one time living in this place was hard —

24
00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.320
precisely because of the lack of proper infrastructure.

25
00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:56.100
But today every resident has at their disposal everything that, for example, any Belgrader has.

26
00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:02.840
Roads, a telecommunications network, internet, stores with everything necessary — all of this is in Sibač.

27
00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:07.360
And yet our hosts stress that they have one advantage that Belgraders don't:

28
00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.980
they don't have constant noise, bustle and numerous stresses.

29
00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:15.220
Branko worked at "Naftagas" his entire working life.

30
00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:19.120
I was a housewife and a peasant.

31
00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:25.140
That's what tied me from childhood until now, and today too.

32
00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.080
In the same way, little by little we do something for ourselves.

33
00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:32.060
Well, it was completely different.

34
00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:35.060
There were some stable prices.

35
00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:40.640
You knew how much pigs fetched, how much corn, wheat, all that.

36
00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:47.100
I sowed melons, then sugar beet, two or three jutros.

37
00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:48.640
Melons two or three jutros.

38
00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:50.660
Potatoes.

39
00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:55.880
For several years we sowed one and a half jutros, like that.

40
00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:58.560
That was our bank at home.

41
00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:01.080
Needless to say about the pigs.

42
00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:04.760
So it happened to us one season:

43
00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:12.240
the beet did well, and I brought it to the scales.

44
00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:18.460
I got 11 million then, went to Dobanovci and drove back a tractor.

45
00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:35.700
Back then it was enough for everything.

46
00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.460
I'll tell you honestly.

47
00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:42.980
Because there wasn't a single gas station.

48
00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:43.940
Everyone came.

49
00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.100
They came from below, from Golubinci.

50
00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:47.300
They came from Dobanovci.

51
00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.020
And then we all knew each other.

52
00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:54.100
And we all socialized.

53
00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:01.340
And now it's somehow weak.

54
00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:06.340
The Nebrigićs have entered retirement waters and live a calm, measured life.

55
00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:07.540
They don't crave money.

56
00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:08.640
And never did.

57
00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:12.640
Happiness for them is a life without stress and with a lot of socializing.

58
00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:15.380
And they have all of this right in this place.

59
00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:18.400
She was from another street.

60
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:20.260
I'm from this street.

61
00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:22.000
I go out on the street.

62
00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.700
I see her below and just wave to her.

63
00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:41.020
And that's when I outwitted her.

64
00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:41.740
Got married.

65
00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:43.860
Thank God.

66
00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:46.480
And how long have you been together?

67
00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:47.420
Married.

68
00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:50.520
You've been together 54 years.

69
00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:50.660
Yes.

70
00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.480
As soon as you step onto this homestead,

71
00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.240
it occurs to you that the saying "everything in perfect order" was coined

72
00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:58.200
just by looking at them.

73
00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:00.740
Not a single thing is out of place.

74
00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:04.300
Every tree, every flower is where it should be,

75
00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:06.700
and complements one idyllic whole.

76
00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:11.380
The credit for all this should be attributed to the female half of this tandem.

77
00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:12.640
Well, you know how?

78
00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:14.260
First, second, third shift.

79
00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:21.440
That is, I mow, and she takes care of the flowers and all that.

80
00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:25.320
Little by little we decorate our garden, our little park.

81
00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:27.820
Sometimes we do it like this: we agree on a day —

82
00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:29.980
on this day we do this — mow,

83
00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:31.860
and tomorrow flowers, like that.

84
00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:34.340
In short, we're here.

85
00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:36.080
And who takes more care of the animals?

86
00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:37.600
Me.

87
00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:40.260
This is my pen, over there and here.

88
00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:43.240
She doesn't allow it, says: this is mine, period.

89
00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.940
In the utility part of the yard the Nebrigić family

90
00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:48.360
raises chickens, pigs,

91
00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:51.960
and most of what they serve at the table

92
00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.880
comes from right here.

93
00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:56.540
Well, when they're slaughtered,

94
00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.080
the same day we salt the meat,

95
00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:00.680
put it in a barrel, in brine,

96
00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:03.440
to stand for three or four weeks,

97
00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:05.920
and then hang it up in the smokehouse.

98
00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:09.940
And before that we make sausages, kulen, blood sausage,

99
00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:12.960
cracklings the same day, like that.

100
00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:14.760
How much does that come to, you have two pigs?

101
00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:16.620
It comes to a lot, three pigs.

102
00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:17.220
You have three pigs?

103
00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:18.860
Three pigs, yes, it comes to a lot.

104
00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:21.500
For almost the whole year.

105
00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:24.000
Yes, not now, now we have two.

106
00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:26.660
Will two be enough for the whole year or not?

107
00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:28.100
Well, it'll be enough.

108
00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:37.340
They wouldn't trade their Sibač and their peace for anything in the world.

109
00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:40.260
That's clear to anyone from a conversation with these lovely people.

110
00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:46.020
Whether it's July, the hottest month, or January, the coldest — it brings a smile to them.

111
00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:51.800
Of course, the smile is in place, because every morning they wake up in this little town and on their own homestead.

112
00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:55.140
If only you could see how good it is here, what peace and quiet.

113
00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:59.200
How you don't have to be nervous from early morning until evening.

114
00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.260
Only the birds can be heard here.

115
00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:16.420
Do you prefer it when it's winter or summer in Sibač?

116
00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:18.440
I don't even know when it's better for us.

117
00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:22.600
In winter we're in the house, our heating works.

118
00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:25.880
Little by little we slice: breakfast, lunch, dinner.

119
00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:30.860
We taste whether it's dry or salty, and so we enjoy.

120
00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:36.100
Life is made up of little things — that's clear from the conversation with the Nebrigić family.

121
00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:39.940
And life in the village sometimes brings a whole handful of pleasant little things.

122
00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:43.040
And that's why the trend that has prevailed for years —

123
00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:46.260
the disappearance of villages and the population leaving rural areas —

124
00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:48.520
seems to us completely unjustified.

125
00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:52.600
After all, the example of this married couple speaks in favor of this claim.